**Fixing line endings in files**

It seems Git might not show significant line diffs, but I need to handle all formatted files, especially if the repo has mixed line endings. I should preserve the no BOM setting. A small PowerShell loop could help convert touched files to CRLF without being destructive. Yet some files might originally be LF. The warnings indicate that LF will be replaced, so I should confirm if `core.autocrlf` is set to true. Ultimately, I want the working tree to use CRLF, so conversion is essential.
